{
  "id": "RADAR-2026-0016",
  "category": "malicious-mcp-server",
  "title": "Apex Foundation republished its macOS dropper under an MCP-branded npm scope after takedown",
  "summary": "From 5 July 2026 an operator branding itself Apex Foundation shipped versions 1.0.0 through 1.0.32 of @apexfdn/apex, an npm postinstall dropper that installs a macOS infostealer, behind a payload-free MCP server published three months earlier as cover. npm removed it on 21 July; within eleven hours the same dropper was live again as @copilot-mcp/apex, a scope borrowing GitHub Copilot's name, and SafeDep counted 20 more versions that day before npm removed that one too.",
